# Namleh Model Bench

Use this to pick the right model for a real Namleh job. Do not benchmark toy
prompts unless the user explicitly asks.

## Candidate Workloads

- Ops Platform feature planning.
- Security/authz review.
- Browser QA interpretation.
- UI/design critique.
- Unity content or tool generation.
- Release notes, handoff docs, and stakeholder summaries.

## Rules

- Never ask for API keys. If a provider is unavailable, report that as setup
  work for Vault or the installed CLI/provider.
- Always run a dry-run or auth/status check before spending model calls.
- Do not enable paid judge/evaluator mode unless the user explicitly approves.
- Save results only when they are useful for future comparisons.

## Command Discovery

Prefer the installed Namleh gstack binary:

```bash
BIN="$HOME/.codex/skills/namleh-gstack/bin/gstack-model-benchmark"
[ -x "$BIN" ] || BIN="./bin/gstack-model-benchmark"
[ -x "$BIN" ] || { echo "gstack-model-benchmark not found"; exit 1; }
```

Run dry-run before real work:

```bash
"$BIN" --prompt "dry run" --models claude,gpt,gemini --dry-run
```

## Benchmark Design

Use a real prompt from the current work. For repeatable comparison, save the
prompt to `.gstack-namleh/benchmarks/prompts/<slug>.md` if the user wants a
baseline.

For each model, judge:

- answer correctness for this repo/business context
- security discipline
- amount of hallucinated process or nonexistent packages
- useful next action
- latency and cost
- whether the output can be handed to Steven or Tim without cleanup

